  "assumptions": [
    "PostgreSQL is the target database; uuid primary keys use gen_random_uuid() (pgcrypto or PostgreSQL 13+), and audit_logs uses a bigint identity key for high-volume append-only inserts.",
    "Every table has exactly one primary key column; junction tables (user_roles, doctor_specialties) use a surrogate id plus a composite unique index on the two foreign keys.",
    "Users can hold multiple roles through user_roles; patient, doctor and staff data live in separate one-to-one profile tables (patients, doctors, staff_profiles) so authentication stays in one place.",
    "Passwords are stored only as bcrypt hashes; reset and verification tokens are stored only as hashes and expire.",
    "Double booking is prevented by the unique (doctor_id, start_at) index on time_slots and a partial unique index on appointments.time_slot_id for active statuses; booking should lock the slot row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) inside a transaction.",
    "Cancelling an appointment sets its status to cancelled and releases the slot (time_slots.status returns to open). Rescheduling creates a new appointment linked through rescheduled_from_appointment_id and marks the old one rescheduled.",
    "The 24-hour cancellation window is enforced in application logic, not by a database constraint.",
    "Weekly availability is stored as recurring rules and materialised into time_slots, so patient searches read pre-generated open slots and changes show up within 1 minute.",
    "Doctor search by name uses users.first_name/last_name, by specialty uses doctor_specialties, and by department uses doctors.department_id. Doctors are deactivated with is_active=false rather than deleted, so history is preserved.",
    "Receptionist bookings use appointments.booked_by_user_id (the receptionist) while patient_id identifies the patient who owns the appointment.",
    "Notifications are queued as rows with status pending and processed by a worker (Twilio for SMS, SMTP for email); receptionists read the status and error_message columns to follow up on failures.",
    "audit_logs rows are append-only and retained for at least 6 years; application database roles should not be granted UPDATE or DELETE on this table.",
    "All timestamps are stored in UTC; time-of-day values in doctor_availability_rules are interpreted in the clinic's local time zone.",
    "Encryption at rest (AES-256) and TLS 1.2+ in transit are handled at the infrastructure/storage layer rather than by schema columns.",
    "Clinical records (diagnoses, prescriptions) are out of scope; appointments.notes holds administrative notes only."
  ]
}